# Repo architecture (ZorbaHealth)

Canonical root is the repo root (`go.mod`, `Tiltfile`, `Makefile`). Do not revive the old `src/` layout.

## Directory ownership

| Path | Owns |
|---|---|
| `services/<name>/` | One microservice |
| `web/` | Next.js frontend only |
| `mobile/` | Expo / React Native client |
| `proto/` | Source `.proto` contracts only |
| `shared/` | Shared Go libs + **generated** protobuf (`shared/proto`) |
| `migrations/` | SQL migrations |
| `deploy/docker|kubernetes|helm/` | Images and cluster manifests |
| `docs/` | Architecture / setup / security truth |
| `scripts/`, `examples/`, `tools/` | Ops helpers, samples, generators |

Run Go/Make/Tilt from repo root. Frontend package commands run from `web/` (or `mobile/`).

## Request and event paths

- **Web/mobile →** `api-gateway` (HTTP) → backend gRPC services. Clients never call internal gRPC directly.
- **Voice →** `voice-agent-service` → `mcp-server` → gRPC backends.
- **Async →** typed RabbitMQ events (`shared/events`, `shared/contracts`). Prefer `patient-service` as publisher for patient workflows; `notification-service` consumes and sends email/SMS.
- **State:** Postgres = durable · Redis = short-lived · RabbitMQ = cross-service events.

## Service boundaries (do not blur)

- `api-gateway` — public HTTP surface only; thin; no domain ownership.
- `auth-service` — accounts, tokens, auth state.
- `patient-service` — patient registration/portal + scheduling / bridged calls.
- `health-records-service` — FHIR/records, embeddings, RAG (`internal/fhir`, `internal/rag`).
- `mcp-server` — tool gateway for voice; consent/audit wrapping; minimal safe context out.
- `audit-service` — append-only audit + consent APIs; owns `audit` schema.
- `notification-service` — RabbitMQ consumers + email/SMS providers + VoIP.ms webhook.
- `location-service` — location sessions / nearest hospital.
- `translation-service` / `interpretation-service` — translation + bridged-call relay.
- `voice-agent-service` — LiveKit agent runtime (Python); not a Go hexagonal twin.
- `health-provider-service` — **stub only**. Do not invent “restore source tree”; hospital/provider flows currently live elsewhere (e.g. auth/api-gateway) until a real service is built.

Legacy stubs without real domain code: do not expand them casually; put logic in the owning service above.

## Go service layout (hexagonal)

Every Go service follows:

```text
services/<name>/
  cmd/<name>/main.go          # wiring only
  config/
  internal/core/domain/       # models, errors — no I/O
  internal/core/ports/        # inbound + outbound interfaces
  internal/core/services/     # use-cases / orchestration
  internal/adapters/primary/  # gRPC, HTTP, RabbitMQ consumers
  internal/adapters/secondary/# DB, providers, publishers, clients
```

Rules:

- Domain and core services depend on **ports**, never on SDKs, SQL drivers, or HTTP clients.
- Provider SDKs live in `internal/adapters/secondary/...` (or `shared/ports/providers` contracts).
- gRPC/HTTP adapters orchestrate; they do not embed business rules or provider SDKs.
- Cross-service calls go through generated clients / ports — not ad-hoc HTTP to another service’s internals.
- Shared helpers: `shared/env`, `shared/logging`, `shared/grpc`, `shared/events`, `shared/db` — prefer these over duplicating.

## Contracts and codegen

1. Edit `.proto` under `proto/` only.
2. Run `make generate-proto` from repo root; commit generated `shared/proto`.
3. Do not hand-edit generated protobuf Go.
4. Schema changes → numbered pair under `migrations/` → regenerate sqlc when queries change.
5. Boundary-changing work updates `docs/architecture.md` and `docs/service-map.md`.

## Feature placement checklist

| Feature type | Put it here |
|---|---|
| New public HTTP route | `api-gateway` + call owning gRPC service |
| Patient/scheduling domain | `patient-service` core + primary gRPC adapter |
| Email/SMS for a workflow | Publish event → `notification-service` consumer (do not SMTP from random services) |
| Voice tool | Thin MCP tool in `mcp-server` → owning service RPC |
| Audit / consent | `audit-service` APIs; emit catalogued event types from `shared/audit` |
| External AI/email/SMS | Secondary adapter + config provider switch |

## Hard bans

- No business logic in `cmd/main.go` or pure wiring packages beyond composition.
- No importing `internal/` of another service.
- No editing generated `shared/proto` by hand.
- No dumping PHI/raw FHIR into logs, MCP tool results, or LLM prompts (use citations / minimal context).
- No new top-level `src/` tree. No putting app code under `deploy/`.
- Do not treat docs “future work” as implemented — verify code and `docs/service-map.md` status.
